================================================================================
Upstream and third-party components
================================================================================

Glasscode is a fork of Zed and reuses Zed's GPUI framework and several of its
supporting crates. We are grateful to the Zed team and contributors.

  Zed — https://github.com/zed-industries/zed
    GPUI and the crates under `vendor/` (gpui, gpui_apple, gpui_macos,
    gpui_macros, gpui_platform, gpui_shared_string, gpui_util, collections,
    http_client, path, perf, refineable, scheduler, sum_tree, util, zlog,
    ztracing, and related) derive from Zed. These are licensed under GPL-3.0 /
    Apache-2.0 as marked in their respective crate manifests and source headers;
    those notices are retained.

The glasses companion app and the voice helper additionally build on:

  Meta Wearables Device Access Toolkit (DAT) for iOS
    https://github.com/facebook/meta-wearables-dat-ios — under its own license.

  ElevenLabs Swift SDK — https://github.com/elevenlabs/elevenlabs-swift-sdk
  LiveKit Swift SDK and WebRTC — https://github.com/livekit/client-sdk-swift

Other dependencies are declared in Cargo.toml / Cargo.lock (Rust) and in the
Swift package manifests, each under its own license.

================================================================================

Glasscode depends on no hosted service of its own. Off-network access is
provided by Tailscale (recommended) or an optional self-hosted relay.
